A||||10||My7Fieros||What could it be!!!??||||8||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-19-2000||08:02 PM||||Heres another redundant question..but this time its REALLY bugging me. Ive got a prob w/ my 87 Gt.....manifolds glow...<BR>Yes yes I know, old problem, but Im about stumped on this one.<BR>Ive replaced the plugs, wires, battery, IAC, replaced the map sensor w/ a used but known good one, rebuilt the distributor (with all new internal pieces)..adjusted the timing SEVERAL times (even pulled the dist twice to make sure it wasnt a tooth off)..<BR>I swear Ive gone over that car w/a fine toothe comb and can find NO vacuum leaks anywhere. <BR>Heres what it does....upon start up, the idle jumps irratically...700-1500 rpms for about the first minute upon start up. It then stabalizes to around 1200 (still too high), and the d*mn manifolds glow! This is getting very nerve racking. Its an 87 Gt w/ 82k on the clock. PLEASE HELP!! TIA, Brian||||reg||8
Z||000001||Jorge||10-19-2000||08:15 PM||||My next step would be to check the cat converter.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Oreif||10-19-2000||08:40 PM||||Did you check the EGR and the EGR tube?<BR>EGR could be patially open or the EGR tube could be cracked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-19-2000||08:50 PM||||My exhaust manifolds glow also when first started, but the car runs fine.  Steady idle 700-900 rpm.   It also is an 87 GT with ~82K miles. I don't know what they do one the car is warmed up.  Exhaust too rich and its burning on the way out?  New cat, new exhaust, wires, distributor etc on mine.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Seanh||10-19-2000||09:57 PM||||I think I would have to agree with Jorge on this one. Sounds like a clogged/bad cat. Converter. Is it just the manifolds that glow, or does the entire exhaust system up to the cat glow? If it glows up to the cat I would definatly think clogged converter is the problem. If it is just the manifold I would think your fuel is running to rich. <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||10-19-2000||10:00 PM||||I checked the egr tube..its fine...<BR>Only the manifolds glow..idle is slighty too hight to..timing is dead on..what gives?<BR>If its running too rich...why?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Seanh||10-19-2000||11:01 PM||||Is the computer throwing out any codes?||||reg||1
Z||000007||007DOUG||10-19-2000||11:14 PM||||Is the computer running in open or closed loop at start-up?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||10-20-2000||12:13 AM||||Somebody told me that it's normal for them to glow sometimes at start-up till idle goes down due to added fuel by the cold start injector.<BR>I've had a few do the same thing, when it's revved and goes closed loop they've stoped glowing.||||reg||1
Z||000009||WisconsinGT||10-20-2000||12:37 AM||||I have a strong gas smell in my 88GT. I have found out that this can happen if (In my case) one of your cylinders has low compression. Apparently, the exhaust gases get backed up and empty out the exhaust. That is what the local GM guy had to say. FWIW||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||10-20-2000||03:04 AM||||Brian, change the cat - BUT - change the O2 sensor at the same time!!! If you don't change the O2 sensor when you change the cat you can burn out the cat in less than 5 miles!! But, to answer your question, the cat is the problem..........oh, if the cat is gone it could have clogged the muffler as well -- ge, it's no wonder your manifolds are glowing!! Hang on, I'm bringing the hot dogs and marshmallows!!!<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                         <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT||||reg||1
